      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before the 1818 Jackson Purchase, the land that is now Drummonds was part of Chickasaw territory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        12,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/drummonds_tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Tipton County was named for Revolutionary War veteran Captain Jacob Tipton, who fell in 1791.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
