      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/drummonds_tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The alluvial soils near the Mississippi River enabled cotton growers in Drummonds to average 1,000 pounds of seed cotton per acre in the 1800s.",
